WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.133 --> 00:00:02.367
-Welcome back.
We're hanging out

00:00:02.367 --> 00:00:04.167
with Aubrey Plaza now.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:04.167 --> 00:00:05.300
Aubrey!
-What?

00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:07.934
-We love getting to know
our guests

00:00:07.934 --> 00:00:09.434
here at "The Tonight Show,"
and I thought it would be fun

00:00:09.434 --> 00:00:10.634
to do it while playing a game.

00:00:10.634 --> 00:00:13.267
It's time to play "Guest Test."
Here we go.

00:00:13.267 --> 00:00:17.300
-♪ Tonight Show Guest Test,
yeah ♪

00:00:17.300 --> 00:00:19.434
-Alright, here's how it works.
Before the show, you answered

00:00:19.434 --> 00:00:21.834
a series of "this or that"
type of questions.

00:00:21.834 --> 00:00:25.234
And now our audience is gonna
try to guess your answers, okay?

00:00:25.234 --> 00:00:27.167
Everyone has clickers
at their seats.

00:00:27.167 --> 00:00:30.501
You can vote for either
answers "A" or "B."

00:00:30.501 --> 00:00:32.300
We're going to do
five questions.

00:00:32.300 --> 00:00:33.968
And here's the deal.
If our audience

00:00:33.968 --> 00:00:36.267
gets at least three questions
right,

00:00:36.267 --> 00:00:39.067
everyone here gets a free pint
of Tonight Dough,

00:00:39.067 --> 00:00:40.467
Ben &amp; Jerry's ice cream.

00:00:40.467 --> 00:00:42.901
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Wow. Wow.

00:00:42.901 --> 00:00:44.801
-Alright, you guys,
how well do we know Aubrey?

00:00:44.801 --> 00:00:46.434
Here we go. Aubrey, ready?
-Okay.

00:00:46.434 --> 00:00:47.667
-Alright.
-What do I do?

00:00:47.667 --> 00:00:49.234
-I'm just going to ask you.
Don't answer yet,

00:00:49.234 --> 00:00:51.334
but we're all going kind of talk
and think about this.

00:00:51.334 --> 00:00:53.601
First question is,
"Pizza or tacos?"

00:00:53.601 --> 00:00:57.000
Now, I know
that you're from New York.

00:00:57.000 --> 00:00:58.334
-Sure. No.
-No?

00:00:58.334 --> 00:01:00.467
-I'm from Delaware.
&gt;&gt; Delaware.

00:01:00.467 --> 00:01:02.567
[ Laughter ]
-Delaware?

00:01:02.567 --> 00:01:05.667
Pizza or tacos, Delaware?
-Scrapple or cheesesteaks.

00:01:05.667 --> 00:01:07.234
[ Laughter ]
-Exactly.

00:01:07.234 --> 00:01:09.734
But you lived in New York.
-I did. I lived in New York.

00:01:09.734 --> 00:01:11.801
-Now you live in L.A.
-And now I live in L.A., yeah.

00:01:11.801 --> 00:01:12.868
Kind of. I don't know.

00:01:12.868 --> 00:01:14.200
-New York has a lot of pizza.
-Yep.

00:01:14.200 --> 00:01:16.467
-L.A. has a lot of tacos.
-Yeah. Yeah.

00:01:16.467 --> 00:01:18.300
-Quest?
-It's hard.

00:01:18.300 --> 00:01:21.167
-I think she's going to
choose tacos.

00:01:21.167 --> 00:01:23.901
-Yeah, but then her accent
in "Emily the Criminal"

00:01:23.901 --> 00:01:25.934
is very New Jersey.
You're kind of like going,

00:01:25.934 --> 00:01:28.334
"Yeah, I didn't want this job."
[ Laughter ]

00:01:28.334 --> 00:01:30.167
I think maybe your research --
-"You looking at me?

00:01:30.167 --> 00:01:31.434
You think
you're better than me?"

00:01:31.434 --> 00:01:32.701
-"You think you're
better than me?"

00:01:32.701 --> 00:01:33.968
And then you add that pizza.
Maybe eat pizza in that.

00:01:33.968 --> 00:01:36.000
So I'm going to say, pizza.
Higgs?

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:37.400
-Pizza.
-Yeah.

00:01:37.400 --> 00:01:39.501
We're gonna say pizza, okay.
Everyone grab your clickers.

00:01:39.501 --> 00:01:41.400
Press "A" for pizza,
"B" for tacos.

00:01:41.400 --> 00:01:43.000
Let's look at the results
right here.

00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:44.801
[ Drum roll ]
-Oh.

00:01:44.801 --> 00:01:46.968
-Barely, pizza!
-Whoo!

00:01:46.968 --> 00:01:49.634
-Aubrey, what was your answer,
pizza or tacos?

00:01:49.634 --> 00:01:51.567
You said...
[ Drum roll ]

00:01:51.567 --> 00:01:53.300
Yeah!
[ Bell ringing ]

00:01:53.300 --> 00:01:55.267
-Come on!
-Yeah!

00:01:55.267 --> 00:01:56.567
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:56.567 --> 00:02:00.901
-Boom! In your face. Yeah!

00:02:00.901 --> 00:02:04.868
-I like pizza. so what?
-So what? So what?

00:02:04.868 --> 00:02:07.000
Get over it.
-Get over it. It's pizza.

00:02:07.000 --> 00:02:09.100
-So close to getting
a free pint of ice cream,

00:02:09.100 --> 00:02:11.601
thanks to Aubrey Plaza.
But who knows what will happen?

00:02:11.601 --> 00:02:13.367
-Ooh.
-The second question.

00:02:13.367 --> 00:02:16.501
You were a former page --
an NBC page here.

00:02:16.501 --> 00:02:17.734
-That's right.
-So my question is,

00:02:17.734 --> 00:02:21.367
"Would you prefer the 1990s
NBC page uniform

00:02:21.367 --> 00:02:24.200
or the current NBC page
uniform?"

00:02:24.200 --> 00:02:25.968
There are the two choices there.

00:02:25.968 --> 00:02:28.601
One had a little more flair.

00:02:28.601 --> 00:02:32.534
-Mm-hmm.
-I kind of like that bow.

00:02:32.534 --> 00:02:33.901
I want to see
what's up with that.

00:02:33.901 --> 00:02:36.501
Where else could you wear it?
-Everywhere.

00:02:36.501 --> 00:02:38.734
-Yeah, you wear it everywhere,
and you show people what's up.

00:02:38.734 --> 00:02:40.467
-Yeah.
-I'm gonna go with

00:02:40.467 --> 00:02:43.801
'90s page uniform.
-Is that thing real?

00:02:43.801 --> 00:02:45.834
-I think she likes
the current one.

00:02:45.834 --> 00:02:48.234
-You think Aubrey likes
the current one?

00:02:48.234 --> 00:02:51.868
I think she's
very pro fashion-forward,

00:02:51.868 --> 00:02:54.200
Aubrey Plaza, and
she would go for that one

00:02:54.200 --> 00:02:56.834
and make that '90s one work.
-With the bow.

00:02:56.834 --> 00:02:58.667
-Yes.
She is not a quitter.

00:02:58.667 --> 00:03:02.334
She doesn't take the easy road.
Yes! '90s page.

00:03:02.334 --> 00:03:03.467
What, you're saying --
-Current. I'm saying current.

00:03:03.467 --> 00:03:06.067
-Alright, everyone,
let's look at the votes.

00:03:06.067 --> 00:03:09.801
The results are in.
Audience said, '90s.

00:03:09.801 --> 00:03:12.601
I'm with the audience.
What did Aubrey say?

00:03:12.601 --> 00:03:14.334
-Whoa!
[ Bell ringing ]

00:03:14.334 --> 00:03:16.334
-'90s!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:16.334 --> 00:03:21.434
[ Laughs ]
-God!

00:03:21.434 --> 00:03:24.834
-Quest. Quest, what's up, man?

00:03:24.834 --> 00:03:26.400
-I thought I knew you.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:26.400 --> 00:03:28.767
-Yeah, because of the bow,
it's fun.

00:03:28.767 --> 00:03:30.100
-Oh, yeah.
I mean, look at me.

00:03:30.100 --> 00:03:31.501
-To dress up.
-I mean, come on.

00:03:31.501 --> 00:03:32.701
-Exactly, you're
a fashion person.

00:03:32.701 --> 00:03:34.200
This is fantastic.
we might be getting

00:03:34.200 --> 00:03:36.467
a free pint of ice cream.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:36.467 --> 00:03:39.701
-Alright, we have three more
questions to go,

00:03:39.701 --> 00:03:41.667
